# Handoff

## 2026-09-02 — Installer hardening merged

- Branch: `main` (PR #4 merged; `004` had already merged as PR #3).
- Current task: none in progress. Specs 001-005 are implemented and on `main`.
- Files modified: see PR #4 — `install.sh`, `google_workspace_admin.py`, `README.md`, `tests/test_setup.py`, `specs/005-installer-hardening/`.
- Tests executed on `main` after merge: unittest suite (13 passed), live `check-setup` (ready, all three commands). The published `install.sh` on `main` is byte-identical to the working tree.
- Known issues: (1) the guided `ensurepip` failure and retry have only been simulated locally with a stub interpreter, never on a real Debian/Ubuntu machine lacking `python3-venv`; (2) an existing `.secrets/token.json` is not migrated into a named profile, by design; (3) `shellcheck` is not installed locally, so only `bash -n` has ever run against `install.sh`.
- Recommended next action: run `curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fishdan/google-ai-admin/main/install.sh | bash` on a clean Debian or Ubuntu machine without `python3-venv` installed, confirm the guided failure message and that installing the package then re-running succeeds, and record the result in progress history.

